{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "kind": "axeyum-settled-fact-statement-pins",
  "note": "SHA-256 of formal.statement for every settled fact. A settled fact's statement is what the ledger CLAIMS; changing it silently turns 'we proved X' into 'we proved something we then labelled X'. Changes require an amendment row below.",
  "amendments": [
    {
      "fact_id": "F:lean-kernel-accepts-the-whole-constructed-real-carrier",
      "date": "2026-08-30",
      "from_sha256": "f96a474ca642f8b9801e4cd4cc8ee2fc6125bfc75a46f4955d495b6a78f295d2",
      "to_sha256": "f24c9a51c52d18c8996e09749143a7ebb324052b193b7745ce0a931a1a91ac25",
      "reason": "OVERCLAIM CORRECTED, NOT A ROUTE UPGRADE. The statement claimed pinned Lean's kernel accepts EVERY declaration of the constructed-real carrier. It does not: `Lean.Environment.addDeclCore` refuses a `theorem` whose type is not a proposition, and this kernel admits 48 of them (plus 25 declarations that depend on one), because `CReal.UniformConvergesOn` is deliberately `Type`-valued. Measured 2026-08-30 by L0/S4's `real_lean_replay_census` and re-measured here: population 2,058, representable 1,985, residue 73. The statement is narrowed to the representable population, with the residue typed, counted and named; nothing was proved that was not proved before, and the claim is strictly weaker. The superseded statement is preserved verbatim in the fact's `notes` AND kept executable as `the_superseded_whole_carrier_claim_is_refuted_by_the_same_binary`, which fails if pinned Lean ever accepts the unfiltered export. The part that is no longer claimed is now the OPEN row `F:lean-kernel-accepts-the-non-prop-residue-of-the-constructed-real-carrier`. ADR-0775; lane `carrier-replay-overclaim`."
    }
  ],
